From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: keep MUTABLE_FORMAT images tiled with UBWC

Adapted from:
https://github.com/Vauzi-17/710/blob/6828465a8bc2ae08b705e4a67a6a2bb76197e231/patches/30-tu-z-mutable.py

On GPUs without ubwc_all_formats_compatible (A722 and A740 included),
upstream drops UBWC and tiling for MUTABLE_FORMAT images whose format list
has component swaps or is missing. TU_Z_MUTABLE picks the behavior:
  0  upstream (linear, no UBWC)
  1  stay tiled, UBWC off
  2  stay tiled, UBWC kept (default)

Tiled images are stored without the component swap, so a view whose swap
differs from the image format reads red as blue. With 1 and 2, an RGBA-type
image with no format list still falls back to linear: shadPS4 creates its
framebuffers that way and renders and samples them through BGRA views.
BGRA-type images with no list stay tiled, which Eden's output images rely
on for speed. R8G8<->R16 reinterpretation always falls back to linear, as
upstream.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 #include "tu_subsampled_image.h"
 #include "tu_wsi.h"
 
+DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(tu_z_mutable, "TU_Z_MUTABLE", 2)
+
 uint32_t
 tu6_plane_count(VkFormat format)
 {
@@ -628,7 +630,8 @@
             ubwc_enabled = false;
             force_linear_tile = true;
          } else if (!mutable_ubwc_fc) {
-            if (ubwc_enabled) {
+            int64_t z_mutable = debug_get_option_tu_z_mutable();
+            if (ubwc_enabled && z_mutable < 2) {
                if (fmt_list && fmt_list->viewFormatCount == 2) {
                   perf_debug(
                      device,
@@ -653,7 +656,18 @@
             bool r8g8_r16 = format_list_reinterprets_r8g8_r16(vk_format_to_pipe_format(image->vk.format), fmt_list);
             bool fmt_list_has_swaps = format_list_has_swaps(fmt_list);
 
-            if (r8g8_r16 || fmt_list_has_swaps) {
+            /* Tiled images are stored without the component swap, so a view
+             * whose swap differs from the image format reads red as blue. With
+             * no format list, an RGBA-type image can be viewed as BGRA (as
+             * shadPS4 does for its framebuffers), so keep upstream's linear
+             * layout for those. BGRA-type images without a list stay tiled.
+             */
+            bool no_list_unswapped =
+               (!fmt_list || !fmt_list->viewFormatCount) &&
+               !tu6_format_texture(vk_format_to_pipe_format(image->vk.format),
+                                   TILE6_LINEAR, false).swap;
+            if (r8g8_r16 ||
+                (fmt_list_has_swaps && (z_mutable < 1 || no_list_unswapped))) {
                ubwc_enabled = false;
                force_linear_tile = true;
             }
